Start accepting connections over one of the two ways in.

wireguard puts a device inside your network: it reaches your NAS,
your printer and this router, as if it were at home.

shadowsocks lends a device this router's way out and nothing else.
It cannot see your network at all — it is for using your own
internet connection from somewhere that is filtering or watching.

olr generates the key or password the first time, so this is also
what makes a configuration or a link possible.

Usage:
  olr remote enable wireguard|shadowsocks [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for enable

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
